<br>
One limit you should know about. The archive publishes unmodified email ori=
ginals so that anyone can verify them independently without relying on my r=
endering of any document. Those files carry their original headers and text=
. Where your names appear in correspondence,
 they remain in those files. They cannot be removed without destroying the =
thing that makes the record verifiable. Identity is not protected there, be=
cause it cannot be. But they are not the kind of files that are automatical=
ly indexed.<br>
<br>
The record is now complete and it is accurate.<br>
